Feature: Agent sheets and gdd agents install
  One data sheet per agent (Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode) says where its commands live, in which
  format, how a command is called and how the recipe starts it headless. `gdd agents install` writes
  the GDD commands into the folder of each agent the project uses (the integrations of
  gdd/models.toml, or the ones named with --agent), and `gdd agents check` says whether they are
  still exactly what gdd would write. Spec Kit is no longer needed.

  Background:
    Given a GDD project in a git repository with the protected paths:
      """
      [protected]
      all = ["gdd/**"]
      """
    And the models:
      """
      [orchestrator]
      integration = "claude"
      model = "opus"

      [builder.yellow]
      integration = "claude"
      model = "sonnet"

      [builder_test]
      integration = "claude"
      model = "sonnet"

      [reviewer]
      integration = "codex"
      model = "gpt-6"
      """

  Scenario: Install writes every GDD command for each agent the models use
    When I run "gdd agents install"
    Then it succeeds
    And the file ".claude/skills/gdd-build/SKILL.md" contains "name: gdd-build"
    And the file ".agents/skills/gdd-review/SKILL.md" contains "VERDICT: OK"
    And the file ".opencode/commands/gdd-build.md" does not exist

  Scenario: Each agent is told how to call the next command its own way
    When I run "gdd agents install"
    Then the file ".claude/skills/gdd-setup/SKILL.md" contains "`/gdd-discover`"
    And the file ".agents/skills/gdd-setup/SKILL.md" contains "`$gdd-discover`"

  Scenario: An agent can be named
    When I run "gdd agents install --agent opencode"
    Then it succeeds
    And the file ".opencode/commands/gdd-status.md" contains "description:"
    And the file ".opencode/commands/gdd-status.md" contains "`/gdd-setup`"
    And the file ".claude/skills/gdd-build/SKILL.md" does not exist

  Scenario: The agent still receives the arguments
    When I run "gdd agents install"
    Then the file ".claude/skills/gdd-review/SKILL.md" contains "$ARGUMENTS"

  Scenario: Written commands say they are generated
    When I run "gdd agents install"
    Then the file ".claude/skills/gdd-learn/SKILL.md" contains "Generated by `gdd agents install`"

  Scenario: Install leaves the agent's other files alone
    Given the file ".claude/skills/my-skill/SKILL.md" says "my own skill"
    When I run "gdd agents install"
    Then the file ".claude/skills/my-skill/SKILL.md" contains "my own skill"

  Scenario: Check passes right after install
    Given I run "gdd agents install"
    When I run "gdd agents check"
    Then it succeeds

  Scenario: Check names a command that was edited by hand
    Given I run "gdd agents install"
    When the change modifies ".claude/skills/gdd-build/SKILL.md"
    And I run "gdd agents check"
    Then it fails with a message that contains ".claude/skills/gdd-build/SKILL.md"

  Scenario: Check names a command that is missing
    Given I run "gdd agents install"
    When the change deletes ".agents/skills/gdd-review/SKILL.md"
    And I run "gdd agents check"
    Then it fails with a message that contains ".agents/skills/gdd-review/SKILL.md"

  Scenario: An agent without a sheet is an error
    When I run "gdd agents install --agent gemini"
    Then it fails with a message that contains "no agent sheet"
